Link with \fI-lexpanse\fR.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBexpanse_set_t\fR is an ordered, dynamic set of 64-bit unsigned integers
(\fBuint64_t\fR), representing a modernized, clean-room equivalent of Judy1.
It scales dynamically across population densities with zero heap allocation for
small populations (immediate word packing) and high cache-line density for
large sparse populations.
.SH QUICK REFERENCE
.nf
.ta 32n 45n
\fBOperation\fR	\fBFunction\fR
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Create / Destroy	expanse_set_new, expanse_set_free
Clear Container	expanse_set_clear
Insert / Remove / Test	expanse_set_insert, expanse_set_remove,
expanse_set_contains
Size & Byte Accounting	expanse_set_len, expanse_set_mem_used
First / Last Key	expanse_set_first, expanse_set_last
Forward Iteration	expanse_set_next_after, expanse_set_next_at_or_after
Reverse Iteration	expanse_set_prev_before, expanse_set_prev_at_or_before
Rank (Count < Key)	expanse_set_count_below, expanse_set_count_range
Select (Nth Key)	expanse_set_by_count (0-based rank)
Batched Prefetch	expanse_set_contains_batch (SIMD/MLP)
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <inttypes.h>
#include <expanse.h>

int main(void) {
    expanse_set_t *set = expanse_set_new();

    /* Insert integer keys */
    expanse_set_insert(set, 10);
    expanse_set_insert(set, 50);
    expanse_set_insert(set, 100);

    /* Membership check */
    if (expanse_set_contains(set, 50)) {
        printf("Set contains 50\\n");
    }

    /* Rank: count keys in [10, 100] */
    printf("Range count [10, 100]: %" PRIu64 "\\n",
           expanse_set_count_range(set, 10, 100));

    /* Select: find the 2nd smallest key (0-based rank, so n = 1) */
    uint64_t second_key;
    if (expanse_set_by_count(set, 1, &second_key)) {
        printf("2nd key: %" PRIu64 "\\n", second_key);
    }

    /* Forward traversal */
    uint64_t k;
    if (expanse_set_first(set, &k)) {
        do {
            printf("  Key: %" PRIu64 "\\n", k);
        } while (expanse_set_next_after(set, k, &k));
    }

    expanse_set_free(set);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SS Example Output
.nf
Set contains 50
Range count [10, 100]: 3
2nd key: 50
  Key: 10
  Key: 50
  Key: 100
.fi
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS Lifecycle
.TP
.BI "expanse_set_t *expanse_set_new(void);"
Allocates and initializes a new empty set handle.
.TP
.BI "void expanse_set_free(expanse_set_t *" set ");"
Frees all memory associated with the set. Passing NULL is a no-op.
.TP
.BI "void expanse_set_clear(expanse_set_t *" set ");"
Removes all keys from the set, resetting it to empty without releasing the
handle.
.SS Mutations & Queries
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_set_insert(expanse_set_t *" set ", uint64_t " key ");"
Inserts \fIkey\fR. Returns \fBtrue\fR if the key was newly added, \fBfalse\fR
if it was already present.
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_set_remove(expanse_set_t *" set ", uint64_t " key ");"
Removes \fIkey\fR. Returns \fBtrue\fR if the key was present and removed,
\fBfalse\fR if absent.
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_set_contains(const expanse_set_t *" set ", uint64_t " key ");"
Returns \fBtrue\fR if \fIkey\fR exists in the set, \fBfalse\fR otherwise.
.TP
.BI "uint64_t expanse_set_len(const expanse_set_t *" set ");"
Returns the total number of keys stored in the set.
.TP
.BI "size_t expanse_set_mem_used(const expanse_set_t *" set ");"
Returns the byte-exact heap memory currently consumed by the set.
.SS Ordered Navigation
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_set_first(const expanse_set_t *" "set" ", uint64_t *"
.BI "key_out" ");"
Writes the smallest key in the set to \fIkey_out\fR. Returns \fBtrue\fR on
success, or \fBfalse\fR if the set is empty.
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_set_last(const expanse_set_t *" "set" ", uint64_t *"
.BI "key_out" ");"
Writes the largest key in the set to \fIkey_out\fR. Returns \fBtrue\fR on
success, or \fBfalse\fR if the set is empty.
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_set_next_after(const expanse_set_t *" "set" ", uint64_t "
.BI "key" ", uint64_t *" "key_out" ");"
Finds the smallest key strictly greater than \fIkey\fR (> key).
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_set_next_at_or_after(const expanse_set_t *" "set"
.BI ", uint64_t " "key" ", uint64_t *" "key_out" ");"
Finds the smallest key greater than or equal to \fIkey\fR (>= key).
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_set_prev_before(const expanse_set_t *" "set" ", uint64_t "
.BI "key" ", uint64_t *" "key_out" ");"
Finds the largest key strictly less than \fIkey\fR (< key).
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_set_prev_at_or_before(const expanse_set_t *" "set"
.BI ", uint64_t " "key" ", uint64_t *" "key_out" ");"
Finds the largest key less than or equal to \fIkey\fR (<= key).
.SS Rank & Select
.TP
.BI "uint64_t expanse_set_count_below(const expanse_set_t *" "set"
.BI ", uint64_t " "key" ");"
Returns the number of keys strictly less than \fIkey\fR in O(depth) time.
.TP
.BI "uint64_t expanse_set_count_range(const expanse_set_t *" "set"
.BI ", uint64_t " "lo" ", uint64_t " "hi" ");"
Returns the number of keys in the inclusive interval [\fIlo\fR, \fIhi\fR].
.TP
.BI "bool expanse_set_by_count(const expanse_set_t *" "set" ", uint64_t " "n"
.BI ", uint64_t *" "key_out" ");"
Selects the key with exactly \fIn\fR keys below it: a \fB0-based\fR rank,
so \fIn\fR = 0 is the smallest key. Writes it to \fIkey_out\fR and returns
\fBtrue\fR, or \fBfalse\fR if \fIn\fR is greater than or equal to the
total population.
.PP
Note this differs from the legacy \fBJudy1ByCount\fR(3), which is 1-based.
.SS Batched Queries
.TP
.BI "size_t expanse_set_contains_batch(const expanse_set_t *" "set"
.BI ", const uint64_t *" "keys" ", bool *" "out_present" ", size_t " "count"
.BI ");"
Executes memory-level parallelism (MLP) prefetching over \fIcount\fR keys.
For each key in \fIkeys\fR[i], writes true/false into \fIout_present\fR[i].
Returns the number of found keys.
